<title>NETHERLANDS: Montell in Saudi venture.</title>
<headline>Montell in Saudi venture.</headline>
<dateline>HOOFDDORP, Netherlands 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Montell Polyelofins said on Monday it had signed a joint venture agreement with Saudi Arabia's Xenel Industries Ltd.</p>
<p>The two partners will establish a company called Teldene, which will construct and operate a propane dehydrogenation plant and polypropylene plant in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia.</p>
<p>Montell is a plastics joint venture between Royal Dutch/Shell and Italy's Montedison  </p>
<p>Half of Teldene will be held by Montell Arabia and the other 50 percent will be owned by NATPET, a group of Saudi investors which includes Xenel Industries Ltd.</p>
<p>No financial details of the cooperation pact were disclosed.</p>
<p>Start-up of the facilities is planned for the year 2000. The polypropylene will be supplied to local Saudi Arabian and regional markets and to Montell's global marketing network, Montell said.</p>
<p>The company added the joint venture would reinforce its strategy of setting up partnerships outside Europe and North America.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
